# A user's global ~/.gitignore may contain `/*` — that happens when the home folder is itself
# a git repository. core.excludesFile applies to EVERY repository, so without this line git
# silently sees none of this project's files and `git add -A` pretends to succeed while
# committing nothing. Measured here: scripts/, commands/ and tests/ were all invisible.
!/*

build/
*.dmg
.DS_Store
node_modules/
# Byte-compiled by the test run; a committed .pyc drifts from its source and is read by nothing
# (the app runs the .py on the system python).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Private maintainer notes (kept out of the public repo)
CLAUDE.md
ROADMAP.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
